  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2024 WA4307 ELRHA UKHIH Responsive Fund Can&apos;t Wait to Learn</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Document Good Practices:&#x202f;Identify transferable examples of good practice in DPL from global and regional DPL to inform education recovery in Gaza.2. Engage Stakeholders:&#x202f;Facilitate consultations with the humanitarian education ecosystem, including the OPT Education Cluster, to gather insights and foster collaboration.3. Assess Risks and Mitigate:&#x202f;Conduct a risk analysis and develop tailored strategies to address political, operational, technological, and sustainability challenges.4. Deliver a Roadmap:&#x202f;Produce a comprehensive report with actionable recommendations and facilitate stakeholder alignment through a dissemination workshop.5. Support Education Recovery:&#x202f;Provide a clear framework for leveraging DPL to improve literacy and numeracy outcomes for children in Gaza.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To identify and assess the risks and opportunities for implementing Digital Personalized Learning (DPL) solutions, such as Can&apos;t Wait to Learn (CWTL), within the Gaza education response, ensuring they are contextually relevant, operationally feasible, and aligned with the needs of children, teachers, and stakeholders to support education recovery in emergencies.</narrative>
  </description>
